    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d26">

                <pb facs="d26-01" n="1" xml:id="d26-01"/>

                <head>26. National Security Study Memorandum 11<anchor n="1" xml:id="d26-f1"/>
                    <anchor n="2" xml:id="d26-f2"/>
                </head>
                <dateline>
                    <placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1969-01-28"
                        >January 28, 1969</date>
                </dateline>
                <list type="to">
                    <head>TO:</head>
                    <item>The Secretary of State</item>
                    <item>The Secretary of Defense</item>
                    <item>The Acting Administrator of AID
                    </item>
                </list>
                <list subtype="subject" type="description">
                    <label>SUBJECT:</label>
                    <item>Nigeria/Biafra Relief</item>
                </list>
                <p>The President has directed the preparation of two papers on the Nigerian civil
                    war. One paper should consider the full range of alternative U.S. approaches and
                    programs aimed at expediting and enlarging urgently the flow of relief to
                    Biafra. This paper should include consideration of coordination, cost, timing
                    and availability of resources.</p>
                <p>The second paper should consider alternative views of U.S. interest in Nigeria
                    and Biafra, the full range of basic policy choices open to the U.S., and the
                    political consequences of alternative approaches to relief described in the
                    first paper.</p>
                <p>The President has directed that the NSC
                    Interdepartmental Group for Africa perform this study.</p>
                <p>Both papers should be forwarded to the NSC Review
                    Group by February 4.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        Henry A. Kissinger
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d26-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d26-f1-content">
                <p>Source: National Archives, Nixon
                    Presidential Materials, NSC Files, NSC Institutional Files (H-Files), Box H–133, NSSM
                    Files, NSSM 11. Secret. A copy was sent to the Chairman of the Joint Chiefs of
                    Staff, General Earle G. Wheeler.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d26-f2" n="2" xml:id="d26-f2-content">
                <p>NSSM 11 directed the preparation of papers on 1) alternative approaches and
                    programs for expanding relief and 2) alternate views of the U.S. interest in
                    Nigeria and Biafra.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
